BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kong Mexico City|AI ROI by Business Unit: FinOps for AI Platforms|
 Online
DTSTART:20261119T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,frontend,web
DESCRIPTION:Kong/MEXICO-CITY\nEvery business unit wants more AI. Finance w
 ants to know what each use case costs and what it returns. When LLM spend 
 arrives as one shared bill\, neither question has a clear answer. This web
 inar shows how to tie AI consumption to the teams and use cases driving it
 . With that view\, leaders can fund what works and rethink what doesn't. W
 e'll walk through how Kong AI Gateway applies team-level token quotas and 
 chargeback attribution at the traffic layer\, before application code touc
 hes a request. You'll see how Konnect Metering & Billing turns that gatewa
 y-native usage data into showback and chargeback reports business owners c
 an trust. We'll also cover how gateway policies can be leveraged to reduce
  the cost of each request. Lower unit costs raise the return on every AI u
 se case you already run. Join us to build an AI cost model that your finan
 ce leaders and your platform team can both stand behind.\n\nKey takeaways:
 \n\n* How to build one AI cost model that finance leaders and platform tea
 ms can both stand behind.\n* How to decide which AI use cases to fund\, sc
 ale\, or rethink using per-team cost and return data.\n* How to enforce AI
  spend limits at the gateway\, before application code touches a request.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Nov 
 19 - Visualizing and Debugging Hugging Face's LeRobot Data|Online
DTSTART:20261119T110000
CATEGORIES:ai,data
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nThis workshop is a hands-on tour of what actually breaks when you load re
 al LeRobot datasets\, and how Voxel51's native LeRobot support in FiftyOne
  catches it.\n\n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nNov 19\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 1
 0:00 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events
 /lerobot-workshop-november-19-2026)**\n\nRobot learning data doesn't look 
 like the data that trains most vision-language models. It's temporal\, low
 -dimensional in the parts that matter most\, embodiment-specific\, and exp
 ensive to collect\, and increasingly\, it's shipped in Hugging Face's LeRo
 bot format. But packaging robot data consistently isn't the same as being 
 able to see it: episodes hide broken metadata\, silently dropped sensor mo
 dalities\, and mismatched schemas between robots that look identical on pa
 per.\n\nStarting from the core differences that make robot data hard (temp
 oral structure\, proprioception\, action grounding\, embodiment heterogene
 ity\, data scarcity)\, we'll move into live debugging: a metadata bug that
  broke multiple dataset imports\, sensor streams that vanish without an er
 ror\, and two robots running an identical benchmark whose data is structur
 ally incompatible. By the end\, you'll know what to check before you trust
  a LeRobot dataset\, and how to actually look inside one.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
